  "solution": "**Given:**\n\n2 ∶ 5, 1 ∶ 2, 8 ∶ 15, 3 ∶ 5 \n\n**Calculations:**\n\nWe need to make the denominator of each fraction same \n\nSo, LCM(5, 2, 15 and 5) = 30\n\nNow, 30/5 = 6,\n\n30/2 = 15,\n\n30/15 = 2 and \n\n30/5 = 6\n\nNow, (2)/(5)×(6)/(6)= (12)/(30),\n\n(1)/(2)×(15)/(15)= (15)/(30),\n\n(8)/(15)×(2)/(2)= (16)/(30)\n\nAnd (3)/(5)×(6)/(6)= (18)/(30)\n\nHence, 18 ∶ 30 = 3 ∶ 5 is the greatest.\n\n**therefore The greatest ratio is 3 ∶ 5.**\n\nf8:T77a,\n<",
